  "rationale": "Exfiltration is not reachable. With mfa_admin and segmented deployed, and every other defence off, the attacker can get partway in: phish_workstation gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user; escalate_workstation gives admin_workstation; pivot_internal then works despite segmentation and gives reach_internal; auth_appserver gives foothold_appserver; kerberoast_dc gives stolen_admin; escalate_appserver gives admin_appserver. Both exfiltration routes, however, need admin_db or admin_fileserver. Those need foothold_db or foothold_fileserver, which need stolen_dbadmin. The only source of stolen_dbadmin is dump_dbadmin_dc, which needs admin_dc, which needs foothold_dc. The only source of foothold_dc is auth_dc, and it requires NOT mfa_admin, so the mfa_admin defence blocks it. The chain breaks there, and exfiltrated stays false."
